  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian political landscape is currently centered on a formal investigation into allegations of illegal wiretapping targeting President Prabowo Subianto. As the investigation progresses, the National Police have formally requested witness protection from the Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK) for six key witnesses to ensure the integrity of the inquiry. Political entities, including the Gerindra Party, have publicly advocated for an expanded scope of investigation to identify all involved parties. High-profile voices, including legal experts, have characterized the potential security breach as a matter of national importance, with some suggesting the actions could be interpreted as treason. Amid these developments, the President hosted ten former chiefs of the National Police for security consultations at his Hambalang estate. Meanwhile, political parties such as Golkar have issued statements warning against unfounded public speculation linking specific political figures to the ongoing surveillance controversy.",
